      "hints": [
        "Integrate $f'(x)$ to get $f(x) = \\frac{1}{12}(4x + 1)^{3/2} - \\frac{3}{2}x + k$.",
        "Substitute $f(0) = -3$ to find $k = -\\frac{37}{12}$.",
        "Evaluate minimum $f(2) = -\\frac{23}{6}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Integrate $f'(x) = \\frac{1}{2}(4x + 1)^{\\frac{1}{2}} - \\frac{3}{2}$ with respect to $x$:\n$$f(x) = \\int \\left(\\frac{1}{2}(4x + 1)^{\\frac{1}{2}} - \\frac{3}{2}\\right) dx = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(4x + 1)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2} \\times 4} - \\frac{3}{2}x + k = \\frac{1}{12}(4x + 1)^{\\frac{3}{2}} - \\frac{3}{2}x + k$$",
        "Use the initial condition $f(0) = -3$ from part (ii) to find $k$:\n$$-3 = \\frac{1}{12}(4(0) + 1)^{\\frac{3}{2}} - \\frac{3}{2}(0) + k = \\frac{1}{12} + k \\implies k = -3 - \\frac{1}{12} = -\\frac{37}{12}$$\n$$f(x) = \\frac{1}{12}(4x + 1)^{\\frac{3}{2}} - \\frac{3}{2}x - \\frac{37}{12}$$",
        "Calculate the minimum value of $f$ at $x = 2$:\n$$f(2) = \\frac{1}{12}(4(2) + 1)^{\\frac{3}{2}} - \\frac{3}{2}(2) - \\frac{37}{12} = \\frac{1}{12}(9^{\\frac{3}{2}}) - 3 - \\frac{37}{12} = \\frac{27}{12} - 3 - \\frac{37}{12}$$\n$$= -\\frac{10}{12} - 3 = -\\frac{5}{6} - \\frac{18}{6} = -\\frac{23}{6} \\quad \\left(= -3\\frac{5}{6} \\approx -3.83\\right)$$"
